{"ev":"session/update","data":{"kind":"agent_message_chunk","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_message_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"# Add a Project README\n\n## Summary\n\nCreate a root-level `README.md` that explains the project’s purpose, prerequisites, usage, and expected output. Base the description on the current implementation: `main.py` prints `hello`.\n\n## Key Changes\n\n- Create `README.md`.\n- Add a concise title and description, using the existing `README.md.bak` text (`tiny project`) only as context.\n- Document the project structure:\n  - `main.py` — prints `hello`\n  - `hello.txt` — contains the auxiliary text `hi`\n- Document how to run the program:\n\n  ```sh\n  python3 main.py\n  ```\n\n- Document expected output:\n\n  ```text\n  hello\n  ```\n\n- Avoid inventing dependencies, installation steps, APIs, or production claims because the repository contains no package metadata or configuration.\n- Leave `README.md.bak` unchanged unless a later cleanup request explicitly asks to remove or rename it.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Confirm `README.md` exists at the repository root.\n- Check that every command in the README works from a clean checkout.\n- Run `python3 main.py` and verify that it outputs exactly `hello`.\n- Review the README for consistency with `main.py` and the current file layout.\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- The README is intended for someone evaluating or running this minimal project.\n- Python 3 is the only prerequisite.\n- `hello.txt` should be documented as a repository file but does not need to be used by `main.py`.\n- No test suite or CI configuration is needed for this documentation-only change.\n"},"messageId":"01a177ec-c956-7711-83ab-e83077e0d452-plan"}}}
